# Canonical author identities.
#
# git consults this when printing names -- shortlog, log and blame all honour
# it by default -- so one person committing under several addresses is counted
# once. It rewrites no history: every commit SHA is unchanged, and a wrong
# entry here is fixed by editing this file.
#
# Line forms in use:
#   Proper Name <email>                      fixes the name for that address
#   Proper Name <canonical> <other-address>  folds an alias onto the canonical
#
# Note GitHub does not read this file; its contributors graph goes off raw
# commit authorship. This governs anything generated from git itself,
# including the contributor list in release notes.
#
# Covers the contributors since the 1.8.3 release. The history before that
# carries roughly 100 distinct identities with a good number still to fold
# in; add them here as they are confirmed rather than guessed.

